>>That said, here are some (IMHO) better PuTTY settings:
>>   Window -> Appearance -> Font: Courier New, Bold, 10 pt
>>   Window -> Translation ->
>>     Received data assumed to be...: CP437
>>     Handling of line drawing characters: Unicode mode
>>Courier New is a 'good Unicode-supporting font', so this sets up all the 
>>  IBMgraphics characters.  (For the last option, 'Unicode mode' is the 
>>default, but I thought I'd best be specific about it.)
> 
> Tried it, and *brrrrr* - I do *not* like the look of the Courier font. 
> It didn't look anything like what the 'good old' Terminal look I like. 

I never liked 10pt Courier New for Nethack, mainly cause I kept running into
floating eyes that I thought were fountains (I was using normal weight, not
bold, so anything dark blue was pretty much invisible). While trying other
fixed-pitch fonts I found that 14pt Lucida Console is very easy to see, and
looks a little bit like Terminal (at least more than Courier New does) - and as
a bonus it's antialiased. Actually, I liked it so much that I use it for all my
PuTTY sessions now...

Warning: some lowercase ascenders are taller than capital letters. I feel that
this makes mind flayers appear more menacing in the rare event that one shows up
in the Gnomish Mines (since 'h' is taller than 'G'). Of course, it does the same
to hobbits...

I use DECgraphics, but it looks like IBMgraphics also works if you use the same
settings samwyse mentions above.

